# InternsHub frontend environment variables
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` (ignored by Git through the `*.local` rule), then uncomment and
# fill in only the values you actually have. Restart `npm run dev` after any change: Vite reads
# these files only at startup.
#
# Every VITE_* value is compiled into the JavaScript bundle and is visible to anyone who opens the
# site. Only put PUBLIC identifiers here. Never add OAuth client secrets, API keys, passwords,
# access tokens or refresh tokens to any VITE_* variable.
#
# The lines below are commented placeholders on purpose: a placeholder client ID would switch on a
# sign-in button that cannot work. Leave a variable commented out until you have the real value.
#
# On Vercel, set the same names under Project Settings > Environment Variables. They are read at
# build time, so a new deployment is needed after changing them.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VITE_API_BASE_URL (optional)
# Origin of the InternsHub backend API, without a trailing slash or /api.
#
# Leave it UNSET locally AND on Vercel. With it unset, the app sends same-origin /api/... requests:
#   - `npm run dev` / `vite preview`: the Vite proxy (vite.config.ts) forwards them to
#     https://api.16-171-93-217.sslip.io.
#   - Vercel (Production and Preview): the /api rewrite in vercel.json forwards them to the same
#     backend, so preview deployments are not blocked by the backend's CORS policy.
# The backend's CORS policy requires requests to go through the proxy to avoid cross-origin
# blocks from non-production origins (localhost, preview deployments).
#
# Set it only to point a build at a different backend that allows your origin through CORS (for
# example a staging API). Ask the backend team for the URL.
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://your-backend.example.com

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# API_PROXY_TARGET (optional; local only)
# Backend that the Vite dev/preview proxy forwards /api/... to. Defaults to
# https://api.16-171-93-217.sslip.io. It has no VITE_ prefix, so it is never compiled into the bundle.
# Not used on Vercel: the /api rewrite destination lives in vercel.json.
# API_PROXY_TARGET=https://api.16-171-93-217.sslip.io

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID (optional; required for "Continue with Google")
# OAuth 2.0 "Web application" client ID from Google Cloud Console > APIs & Services > Credentials.
# It is a public identifier, not the client secret. Never add the secret here.
# Use the same client ID the backend validates Google ID tokens against
# (POST /api/auth/external/google), so get it from the backend team.
# Its "Authorized JavaScript origins" must include every origin that shows the button, for example
# http://localhost:5173 and https://internshub-official.vercel.app.
# Without it, the Google button shows "Google sign-in isn't available yet."
# VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=<google-web-client-id>.apps.googleusercontent.com

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VITE_MICROSOFT_CLIENT_ID (optional; required for "Continue with Microsoft")
# Application (client) ID of the Azure / Microsoft Entra app registration, a GUID shown on the
# app's Overview page. It is a public identifier. Never add a client secret here.
# It must be the app whose ID tokens the backend accepts (POST /api/auth/external/microsoft), so get
# it from the backend team or the Azure admin.
# The app registration must list these as "Single-page application" redirect URIs, with ID tokens
# enabled:
#   http://localhost:5173/auth/microsoft/callback        (local dev; match your dev port)
#   https://internshub-official.vercel.app/auth/microsoft/callback
# Without it, the Microsoft button shows "Microsoft sign-in isn't configured for this site yet."
# On Vercel, set it (and VITE_MICROSOFT_TENANT_ID) for both Production and Preview. Azure matches
# redirect URIs exactly, so sign-in works only on origins listed above; a Preview deployment URL
# must be added to the app registration before Microsoft sign-in works there.
# VITE_MICROSOFT_CLIENT_ID=<azure-application-client-id-guid>

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VITE_MICROSOFT_TENANT_ID (optional)
# Which Microsoft accounts may sign in. Defaults to "common" (work, school and personal accounts)
# when unset. Use "organizations", "consumers" or a specific tenant GUID only if the Azure app
# registration is limited to that audience. Ask the Azure admin which one the app supports.
# On Vercel, set it for both Production and Preview, next to VITE_MICROSOFT_CLIENT_ID.
# VITE_MICROSOFT_TENANT_ID=common
